  <uml:Package xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1501686483781_425073_24619" xmi:uuid="a9f59986-2d75-40b7-b9d9-c630cdbe76cb" xmi:type="uml:Package">
    <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1512144797207_202198_39063" xmi:uuid="124aaa5b-c9d8-4881-a6b0-5357cc8d66a8" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
      <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1501686483781_425073_24619"/>
      <body>This capability contains basic topological entities and specialized subtypes independent of a specific usage or geometry.&lt;br&gt; The main topological entities are Vertex and Edge that is connecting two vertices.&lt;br&gt; Edges can be combined into a Path or into ConnectedEdgeSet.&lt;br&gt; SubEdge can be defined by introducing additional vertices on the parent Edge and be used in further subsets of a ConnectedEdgeSet.&lt;br&gt; Entities can be shared by several Representations when they belong to the same RepresentationContext.&lt;br&gt; EdgeBasedTopologicalRepresentationWithLengthConstraint is such a Representation that contains only topological entities and is defined by unspecific points and curves that are independent of any specific coordinates. Only the lengths of the curves are constrained to specific values. </body>
    </ownedComment>
